    "comments": [
      {
        "id": "comment-1",
        "text": "ADVANCED 5/9: CLASS INHERITANCE (the base)\nAdvEnemyBase defines the CONTRACT every enemy follows: `take_damage(amount)` reduces health by the\namount minus armor (never less than 1) and raises `died` at zero. Subclasses such as\nAdvEnemyBoss keep these two events and add behaviour. Open AdvEnemyBoss to see the extension.",
        "position": [
          0,
          -270
        ],
        "size": [
          1500,
          170
        ],
        "color": [
          0.9,
          0.75,
          0.2,
          0.28
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": []
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-2",
        "text": "1. BEGIN PLAY - announce the spawn.",
        "position": [
          -40,
          -80
        ],
        "size": [
          680,
          270
        ],
        "color": [
          0.25,
          0.45,
          0.75,
          0.22
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "bp",
          "bp_log"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-3",
        "text": "2. THE CONTRACT: take_damage(amount) - damage reduced by armor with a floor of 1\n(Max(amount - armor, 1) so a high armor never makes the enemy immortal), subtracted from health,\nand `died` is dispatched at zero or below.",
        "position": [
          -30,
          390
        ],
        "size": [
          3040,
          710
        ],
        "color": [
          0.25,
          0.65,
          0.35,
          0.22
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "td",
          "td_armor",
          "td_sub",
          "td_max",
          "td_hp",
          "td_hp_sub",
          "td_set",
          "td_dead",
          "td_if",
          "td_died"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-4",
        "text": "3. DEATH - log and remove this object from the world (its own entity comes from this class's\nTransform). Subclasses may replace this: a boss would also drop loot.",
        "position": [
          -40,
          1760
        ],
